        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-26T19:58:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For the specific case of a PR_SWAP, we should be setting our CC to Rd, correct? \n\nI definitely understand your unease here though.  If, for example, we ended up in a scenario where we started an AMS and never transitioned out of/back into our ready state then we could inadvertently leave NG set and block all sink attempts at starting an AMS.  I checked the code and I don\u0027t believe we have any messages that currently do this (with the exception of ping, which isn\u0027t listed as an AMS anywhere I can find).\n\nIt does occur to me that we should probably be setting SINK_TX_OK when an AMS start message send fails.  I\u0027ll work on that.",
      "parentUuid": "e2a11959_e2aae672",
